The level parallel with the first level of the mines is certainly easier
than the first level of the mines: fewer monsters and most of it will be
lit. The former is due to the surface area that monsters can appear. You
can dwell on a level if you see your hp going up and down a *lot*. i.e.
you have to pray for HP. If you build up your bare-handed fighting, you
will have to worry less about traps in the mines, as then your weapon
won't be affected, just the amount you're hit. Build up your missile
weapon skill, preferably on F's and e's eat the later and hopefully you
can find a (uncursed) blindfold or towel. By that point you should have
at least 50 hp and 0 AC or lower. You are far safer in the mines with
skilled ability in at least your melee weapon. Don't worry about spells
until you have an AC arround -5 or more. At that point you will have
found some non-metal armor and hopefully the means to enchant/protect
your weapon(s) and armor. 

